0px solid white; ">2</td><td align="center" colspan="2" style="border: 0px solid white; ">3</td><td align="center" colspan="2" style="border: 0px solid white; ">4</td><td align="center" colspan="2" style="border: 0px solid white; ">5</td><td align="center" colspan="2" style="border: 0px solid white; ">6</td><td align="center" colspan="2" style="border: 0px solid white; ">7</td><td align="center" colspan="2" style="border: 0px solid white; ">8</td><td align="center" colspan="2" style="border: 0px solid white; ">9</td><td align="center" colspan="2" style="border: 0px solid white; ">10</td><td style="border: 0px solid white; "></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Two (2) distinct types of restriction enzyme recognition sites, <i>VspI</i> and <i>ZrmI</i>, are labeled at the top of this DNA segment.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> The dashes at both ends of the strand indicate that the next restriction site is far away and outside the visible region. Because this segment is part of a much larger molecule, any uncut or very large fragments will not travel into the gel and will appear to be stuck in the well.</p><h6><strong>Determine the sizes of the DNA bands</strong> that would appear on an agarose gel after digestion with <i>VspI</i> only.</h6>
PROMPT_18D6_3635
loadMacros('parserCheckboxList.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_1';
1 kb
LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_2';
2 kb
LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_3';
3 kb
LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_4';
4 kb
LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_5';
5 kb
LITERAL_18D6_3635_CHOICE_5
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_18D6_3635_CORRECT_1';
3 kb
LITERAL_18D6_3635_CORRECT_1
$correct_2 = <<'LITERAL_18D6_3635_CORRECT_2';
4 kb
LITERAL_18D6_3635_CORRECT_2
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5);
@correct = ($correct_1, $correct_2);
$answer = CheckboxList([@choices], [@correct], labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
BEGIN_TEXT
\{$answer->checks\}
END_TEXT
ANS($answer->cmp);

ENDDOCUMENT();
